// models/concepts.memql -- the curated model catalog (epic memql#5137, D1).
//
// WHAT THIS IS AND IS NOT. The catalog says what a machine SHOULD pull, by
// category and by machine class. It gates nothing. Eligibility for a call is
// what a machine ADVERTISES on its registration label (`model:<id>` with
// ctx=, structured=, tools=, vision=, ...), which is a fact about a running
// process; a profile here is a recommendation about a model, which is a fact
// about weights. Conflating the two would let a catalog entry make a machine
// eligible for work it cannot do, and the failure lands on somebody's laptop
// three layers from the decision.
//
// WHY DSL DATA RATHER THAN A LIST IN GO. A model is a data change now, not a
// release. The alternative considered and rejected in D1 was an unbounded
// mirror of the Ollama library: the owner asked for the best few entries per
// category, and a mirror is a different product -- it answers "what exists"
// where the question is "what should I run".

/// A curated model the catalog recommends, by category and machine class.
///
/// TIER: public, requiresIdentity. Any signed-in person reads it. The Fleet models surface has to
/// say what this fleet COULD run before anybody has pulled anything, and a catalog narrowed by owner
/// would show a new operator an empty page with no way to tell that from "nothing is recommended".
/// There is nothing here to protect: every row is a public model id and a published size.
@rowAuthz(public, requiresIdentity)
@displayCard(primary="modelId", secondary="category", tertiary="runtime", status="curated")
concept modelProfile {
  modelId          string!  @description("The runtime's own id, byte-identical to what a machine advertises as `model:<id>` -- an Ollama tag (qwen3.5:9b) or hf.co/<owner>/<repo>. A catalog hit is therefore a string equality and never a fuzzy match, which is what stops qwen3.5:9b and qwen3.5:9b-q4 from being read as one model. NOT the row id: a tag carries ':' and '/', and the canonical row id is {concept}:{shortId}, so the row id is a slug of this and this is the field everything compares on.")
  category         enum("text", "reasoning", "omni", "vision", "audioIn", "audioOut", "imageGen", "videoGen", "embeddings")!  @description("What the model is FOR. Streaming is deliberately absent and is a flag instead: it is true of models in every category, and a category for it would put one model in two rows -- the exact shape the vendor provider records are losing in this epic. `vision` is a category for a model whose PURPOSE is seeing; a text model that can also see carries the flag and stays in `text`.")
  runtime          enum("ollama", "mlx", "whispercpp", "nemo", "kokoro", "mflux", "comfyui")!  @description("Which runtime serves it. A machine lacking the runtime cannot pull the model at all, which is one of the three reasons the Fleet page gives for a profile this fleet cannot serve. The set is closed because each value is a thing the cockpit knows how to install; a runtime nobody installs is not a recommendation.")
  family           string   @description("The model family (qwen3.5, gemma4, gpt-oss), for grouping on a page. Not parsed from modelId: the tag's shape is the runtime's business and has changed before.")
  params           int      @description("Parameter count expanded to a number (9B -> 9000000000). Zero means the publisher did not state one -- an ORDERING signal, never a capability gate, the same rule fleetModel.params follows.")
  quant            string   @description("The quantization the recommended tag carries (Q4_K_M, Q8_0, MXFP4). Precision breaks recommendation ties between otherwise equal parameter counts, so larger memory classes can choose the higher-precision tag without inventing a different parameter count.")
  sizeBytes        int      @description("Download size of the recommended tag as the library reported it on the day of seeding. Zero means it was not stated there -- and a zero is left as a zero rather than estimated, because a made-up download size is indistinguishable on a page from a measured one.")
  memoryNeedBytes  int      @description("The catalog's resident-memory allowance at the working context and quantization documented in the seed notes, including weights, KV cache and runtime buffers. Curation records estimates and measurement provenance with the seeds; this is a budget, not a promise of free memory on a machine. Zero means not estimated. minMachineClass decides where a model is offered, and the curated set must fit that class's combined budget.")
  contextWindow    int      @description("The catalog's context ceiling in tokens, which may be capped below the model's published maximum. The working context used for the resident-memory allowance is documented separately in the seed notes. Actual routing eligibility comes from the runtime's advertised context. Zero means not stated.")
  flags            []string @description("What the MODEL can do, as the subset of {structured, tools, thinking, vision, audioIn, audioOut, imageGen, streaming} that is TRUE. A LIST rather than an object of booleans, and absence rather than false, for the same reason the registration label omits a flag it does not advertise: the two vocabularies are deliberately the same eight words, and making the two spellings the same shape is what lets the Fleet page compare a profile against a machine without translating. A model listing a flag and a machine not advertising it is the ORDINARY case -- the runtime behind an endpoint is half of every one of these capabilities.")
  dimensions       int      @description("Vector width, for an embeddings entry; zero for every other category. This is the field that makes the embedder binding's width a fact about the PROVIDER rather than a constant in the schema (memql#5142), so an embeddings entry without it is refused by the seed gate -- a binding cannot create its table without knowing the width.")
  license          string   @description("The weights' licence (apache-2.0, mit, gemma, qwen). Recorded because a person choosing what to run on hardware they own is entitled to know what they are agreeing to, and because two entries in one category can differ on exactly this.")
  source           string   @description("URL of the library or vendor page this entry was verified against, on the day it was seeded. Curation is a release-time act and this is its receipt.")
  recommendedFor   []string @description("Levels this model is a good answer for: fast | strong | reasoning | embeddings. EMPTY means listed and recommended for nothing, which is how videoGen is honest: the catalog names those models so an operator can see they exist and were considered, and recommends them nowhere.")
  minMachineClass  enum("16", "24", "32", "64", "128")!  @description("Gigabytes of unified memory or VRAM below which this model does not run usefully. A machine's recommended set is every profile whose class it meets. A declared floor rather than a computed one: the computation needs a measurement nobody has taken yet, and a floor that is wrong in the permissive direction is a model that swaps to disk on somebody's laptop.")
  offeredOn        []string @description("macos | linux. A videoGen entry is linux-only and SAYS so, rather than being absent on a Mac and unexplained -- the third of the three reasons the Fleet page gives for a profile this fleet cannot serve.")
  notes            string   @description("One sentence for an operator: what this entry is the best pick FOR. The catalog is a recommendation and a recommendation with no reason is a preference.")
  measured         object   @description("Empty until epic memql#5146. Measured throughput and quality with provenance. The catalog ranks nothing on it this release, and an empty object here is 'nobody has measured this', never 'it measured zero'.")
  active           bool  @description("False once an operator removed their entry. A soft delete, because the row is the record that somebody added this id and then took it out again; a hard delete leaves the next operator asking the same question with nothing to read. Separate from `unavailable` on purpose -- that one is about the world (the runtime stopped serving the id), this one is about the operator's list.")
  curated          bool  @description("False for an entry an operator added by id. A curated entry is a release-time act re-seeded on every boot; an operator's entry is theirs and is not re-seeded, which is also why modelProfileRemove refuses a curated row -- removing one is a lie the next restart undoes.")
  unavailable      bool @description("Set when a pull failed because the runtime no longer serves the id. The row STAYS and says so rather than vanishing: curation is a release-time act, and a catalog entry that disappeared answers 'why can I not pull this' with silence.")
}
